## Practical Tips for Your Trip

| Topic | Recommendation |
|-------|----------------|
| **Transportation** | • **Kunming City**: Use the metro (Line 1 & 2) or ride‑hailing apps (DiDi). <br>• **Stone Forest & Dianchi Lake**: Rent a car or join a day‑tour group; the drive takes ~1.5 h each way. <br>• **Shangri‑La**: Bus or private transfer; the drive takes ~4 h. |
| **Weather** | Kunming is known as the “City of Eternal Spring.” Expect mild temperatures (15–25 °C) year‑round, but it can rain in the summer (June–August). Pack a light rain jacket. |
| **Language** | Mandarin is the official language. English signage is common in tourist spots, but learning a few basic Chinese phrases (e.g., “Nǐ hǎo” – hello, “Xièxiè” – thank you) can be helpful. |
| **Currency** | The local currency is the Chinese Yuan (RMB). Credit cards are accepted in most hotels and larger restaurants; carry some cash for smaller shops and street vendors. |
| **Health & Safety** | • Stay hydrated, especially when walking long distances. <br>• Use bottled water for drinking; tap water is not recommended for tourists. |
| **Tickets & Reservations** | • For popular sites like the Stone Forest, book tickets online in advance to avoid long queues. <br>• Some attractions (e.g., Kunming Zoo) offer free entry for children under 12. |
| **Cultural Etiquette** | • Dress modestly when visiting temples. <br>• Remove shoes before entering temple halls. <br>• Respect local customs and avoid loud conversations in quiet areas. |

